  "@type": "Process",
  "critical": false,
  "description": "Physical Vapor Deposition (PVD): sputtering (DC, RF, magnetron) and evaporation (thermal, electron-beam) of metal and dielectric thin films in high vacuum. Chamber pressure ~10⁻³ Torr (sputtering with Ar) or 10⁻⁶–10⁻⁸ Torr (evaporation). Deposits Al, Ti, Cu, Ta, W, and other target materials as conductive, barrier, or adhesion layers for IC metallization. Film thickness monitored by quartz crystal microbalance (QCM).",
  "early_win": false,
